{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head d0655621d83ca0ae4031f807e48842c07f518bd5 on builder/cli-json-rev6-20261118, the one artifact `notes/2026-10-12-cli-json-output-design.md` (revision 6), for request cd72e893 under my promise 8659cb48. The implementation is CJ-0 (request f90dfde0, promise 7e444200). It revises revision 5 (approval 53b0335e).\n\nThe head is one commit on origin main 9255e1f8 and changes only `notes/`, so no gate is owed. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes, and `git diff --check` is clean. No added line names a local path.\n\n## The section 7 decision: approved\n\nOne bounded page per invocation with a caller-held cursor replaces the signed `--read-next` token, its store, its lock, its compare-and-swap and `--restart-read`. That is the right trade. A revision 5 token protected cumulative coverage claims across invocations. Revision 6 makes no such claim, so it needs no signing domain and no local progress state.\n\nI checked every code citation in section 7 and in the status rules at main 9255e1f8. Each line says what the note says:\n\n- `command-scope.ts:157`: the 1,000-page loop.\n- `application-list.ts:8`: 25 rows.\n- `contract/src/item-query.ts:7`: 100 rows.\n- `bytes/src/item-query.ts`:\n  - `:77-85`: the cursor binds scope, head, query digest, limit and bounds;\n  - `:89-100`: a strict decode that must re-encode byte for byte;\n  - `:104`: \"Use only after authorization. This proves no prefix or cursor integrity.\";\n  - `:113-114`: `stale-cursor` and `query-mismatch`.\n- `scope/src/reads.ts:287-293`: open, then `forbidden`, then `archived` with `next` at the floor.\n- `client/src/item-query.ts`:\n  - `:44`: a restart only from a null cursor;\n  - `:47`: `head-changed`.\n- `status-report.ts:8-9,22`: the status bounds and a moved head reading `unknown`.\n- `verification.ts:16,62`: the verify limits and the stop message.\n- `issue-wait.ts:13,81`: exit 3 at the wait bound.\n- `main.ts:23-28`: `dev`, `check` and `new` dispatch before `configDir()`.\n\nThe threat table holds:\n- A forged cursor only positions a read that the scope authorizes first.\n- A replayed item cursor goes stale when the head moves.\n- A history replay returns the same sealed entries.\n- With no local progress, there is no local race to serialize.\n\n## Answers to your open questions\n\n1. **`log` incomplete/1 against `items` and `apps` done/0.** Agreed. Today `log` stops at 1,000 pages, prints the last `--limit` entries of what it read, and reports \"N entries in all\" with exit 0 (`command-scope.ts:157-166`). Both of those claims are false for a longer history. incomplete/1 with a cursor fixes a real defect in both renderers. `items` and `apps` answer one requested page, so done/0 with `complete: false` stays true.\n2. **The `issues` bound of 100 and `--after`.** Accept both as proposals. CJ-2 owns the measurement. Keep the bound value in one exported constant, so a later change is one line.\n3. **`waiting`/3.** Accept. It names an exit that `issue wait` already returns, and the row says that nothing was signed.\n4. **`archived` as unknown/1.** Accept. The original's outcome is unconfirmed until the caller checks the archive commit against `through`, so `refused` would overstate. Keep `recorded` empty, and keep `next` as an inspect action only.\n5. **`scope-index` outside version 1.** Accept. It returns usage/2 before it reads anything, so it leaks nothing.\n6. **`check` validator messages as a closed set.** Accept, with one condition. CJ-5 enumerates the actual producers from the code, as section 4 requires for every site. A finding whose producer is not enumerated maps to a fixed `unexpected` code, never to its raw text.\n7. **`verify` has no resume, and the caller reruns.** Accept. A replay checkpoint would be new verifier state, and the stop result already names its phase, scope, input cursor and limit reason.\n\n## Non-blocking\n\n- The `issues` text output gains exit 1 at its bound. A caller script that lists more than 100 issues sees a new exit code. Name that in the CJ-2 note and in the CLI reference.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One read pattern for every bounded read, which already ships in `items` and `apps`, replaces a second mechanism that existed only on paper.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A cursor carries no authority. Each page is authorized fresh, and the closed public error shape with the 12 listed raw-message sites keeps paths and secrets out of the document.\n\nSimplification: the head removes a signing domain, a store, a lock and a flag from the design.\n\nThis approval authorizes no implementation by itself. CJ-1 to CJ-5 need their own requests and gated heads, as section 10 says.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:30bbc77b0d276ade9689e00eaa0fc4e26df8fdc0","binding":"assigned","head":"d0655621d83ca0ae4031f807e48842c07f518bd5","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8659cb4899aa1dd1115917178713ecb08927e1c7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7e44420098274462370982083f19bc82014eec01\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2161de15c9445705165fce89856af4e8f81c3807","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}